# 💎 Skill: Impeccable (Production-Grade UI/UX Craft & Anti-AI-Slop)

Use when designing, auditing, polishing, refining, or adapting any frontend interface in `client/src/`.

## 1. Absolute Design Bans (Anti-AI-Slop Rules)
- **NO Side-stripe borders:** Do not use `border-left` or `border-right` > 1px as colored accents on cards.
- **NO Gradient text:** Avoid `background-clip: text` combined with gradients. Use solid high-contrast colors.
- **NO Decorative Grid Overlays:** Avoid arbitrary line background grids unless building a drawing canvas.
- **NO Excessive Border Radius:** Cards top out at 12–16px (`rounded-xl` / `rounded-2xl`). Do not use 32px+ on standard cards.
- **NO Low-Contrast Text:** Body text must hit ≥4.5:1 against its background. Do not use washed-out muted gray text on near-black.

## 2. Layout & Typography Rules
- **Line Length:** Cap body line length at 65–75ch for optimal readability.
- **Headings:** Balance title wrapping using `text-wrap: balance` on H1–H3.
- **Display Tracking:** Display heading letter-spacing floor: ≥ -0.04em. Never cramp letter spacing below -0.04em.
- **Grid Layouts:** Use `repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr))` for responsive flex grids.

## 3. Motion & Micro-Interactions
- **Exponential Easing:** Use smooth exponential ease-out curves (`ease-out-quart`, 150-200ms).
- **Tactile Feedback:** Buttons and interactive cards must have subtle active states (`active:scale-95 transition-all`).
- **Accessibility (a11y):** Respect `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)` for all entrance animations.

## 4. Accessibility (a11y)
- Ensure all interactive elements have keyboard focus rings (`focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-emerald-500`).
- Use native semantic HTML elements (`<button>`, `<main>`, `<header>`, `<section>`).
